---
title: How to Connect a CalDAV Calendar
description: >-
  Connect a CalDAV calendar such as iCloud, Nextcloud or Fastmail so your
  bookings appear on it and its events appear in Taskip.
sidebar:
  order: 12
---
**A CalDAV calendar works in both directions. Taskip writes your events and bookings to it, and events you add in your desktop calendar app show up in the Taskip calendar.**

### **Connect the Calendar**

1. Go to **Settings → Meeting Settings → Integrations**.
1. Find **CalDAV calendar** and click **Connect calendar**.
1. Enter the **Server URL**. It must start with `https://`.
1. Enter your **Username** and **Password**. Use an app password if your provider offers one.
1. Click **Find calendars**.
1. Pick the calendar from **Calendars found**.
1. Optional: give it a **Name**.
1. Click **Connect**.

Taskip checks that it can write to the calendar before it saves the connection. If it cannot, you see the reason and nothing is saved.

Each connected calendar is listed with its status (**Active** or **Error**) and when it was **Last checked**. Click **Test** to check it again, or **Remove** to disconnect it.

### **Send Events to the Calendar**

- On any event, turn on **Add to CalDAV calendar** and pick the calendar. See [How to Use the Meeting Calendar](/meeting-scheduler/how-to-use-the-meeting-calendar/).
- To write **every booking** to a calendar, use **Also add every booking to…** on the same Integrations page. Choose a Google Calendar or a CalDAV calendar and click **Save**. Choose **Don't add** to turn it off.

New, rescheduled and canceled bookings are kept up to date on that calendar.

### **See Your Desktop Calendar Events in Taskip**

Events you add in your calendar app, such as Apple Calendar or Thunderbird, appear in the **Calendar** tab of Meetings.

- **When** – when you open the Calendar tab, Taskip reads each connected calendar in the background, at most once every 5 minutes. The events appear a few seconds later, and the tab refreshes once by itself.
- **How far** – events from 14 days back to 180 days ahead.
- **Read-only** – these events cannot be edited, rescheduled or canceled in Taskip, and no invites or reminders are sent for them. Change them in your calendar app.
- **Changes** – if you move or edit an event in your calendar app, Taskip updates it. If you delete or cancel it there, it disappears from Taskip.
- **Repeating events** – each occurrence appears on its own day. An event that runs over several days appears on each day.
- **Time zone** – times are shown in your workspace time zone.
- **No duplicates** – events Taskip itself wrote to the calendar are not read back in.
- **Format** – an event with an address shows as **In person**. Anything else shows as **No format**.

{% table %}
---
- **Note:** Every connected CalDAV calendar is read, including one you connected only to send bookings to. Removing the connection also removes the events that were read from it.
{% /table %}

### **If Something Goes Wrong**

- If a calendar shows **Error**, click **Test** to see the reason, then check the server address, username and password.
- A failed read keeps the events already in Taskip. The next read tries again.
- The server must be reachable over `https://` on the public internet.
